chapter.v:
	For though 

	 I am free from all men, I have made myself a servant to all, that I might win the more;
 [Rom. 16:5]

	and to 

	 the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might win Jews; to those who are under the law, as under the law, that I might win those who are under the law;
 [Rom. 16:16]

	to those 

	 who are without law, as without law (not being without law toward God, but under law toward Christ), that I might win those who are without law;
 [Rom. 16:22;]
